---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from './Eyebrow.astro';

const frameworks = [
  'EU AI Act Art. 12 & 14',
  'NIST AI agent standards',
  'CSA agentic trust',
];
---

<Section id="the-record">
  <Eyebrow class="reveal">The record</Eyebrow>

  <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">Prove a human oversaw the machine.</h2>

  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.4fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <p class="reveal text-[17px] leading-[1.62]">
      From December 2027 the EU AI Act requires logged, documented human oversight of
      high-risk AI systems. Singapore&rsquo;s IMDA framework already requires an audit
      trail of which agent acted under whose authority. Assay produces a signed
      attestation for every AI-authored change: which agent wrote it, what authority it
      held, what verified it, and who approved. Independence is the part nobody can
      self-certify.
    </p>

    <ul class="reveal flex flex-wrap content-start gap-2.5 lg:pt-1" style="--reveal-delay:60ms">
      {
        frameworks.map((name) => (
          <li>
            <span class="chip uppercase tracking-[0.1em]">{name}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</Section>
